# Two declaration slots interleaved, so the rule's find order is exercised across BOTH node kinds
# rather than within one. The three declarations below are `define repeat`, then `struct if`, then
# `define while`, and the three findings MUST come out in that order. This is the guard the
# `.sort(compareBySpanStart)` used to provide; issue #837 removed the sort when procedure PARAMETERS
# stopped being checked (that was its only out-of-order case), leaving the walk's pre-order to carry
# the promise on its own -- so the promise needs a mixed-kind fixture to stay honest.
define repeat
  print 1
end
struct if [ x y ]
define while
  print 2
end
